<!--
  SecretPrinter.Loop6.csproj

  Written by Claude (Anthropic model, Claude Opus 5) at the direction of
  Edwin West, 2026-09-14, for the SecretPrinter project. Reviewed by a human
  before merge.

  A loopback measurement. It answers one question that SecretPrinter.Listen6
  cannot: when this host sends to ff02::fb and the operating system loops a copy
  back to a socket joined on a real adapter, what interface index does
  IPV6_PKTINFO report for that copy?

  The answer decides whether the socket half of REQ-ADV-018 and REQ-ADV-020 can
  be covered by a test that sends to the group and asserts arrival, or whether
  that test design is unavailable. It is being run before the receive code is
  written, because it changes what that code must expose.

  Unlike Listen6, this tool SENDS. At its default hop limit of 0 the datagram is
  expected to stay on this host; the program says on screen what it is about to
  put on the network before it does it. See the Program.cs header.

  Deliberately carries no Requirement markers, for the same reason as
  SecretPrinter.Listen, Listen6, Respond and Respond6: the requirements in
  README.md describe the service. A marker here would make the coverage matrix
  report a service behaviour when what exists is a measurement of the operating
  system.

  No project references and no NuGet packages. The receiving socket's
  configuration is written out in full rather than shared with
  SecretPrinter.Mdns, so that the thing being measured cannot silently change
  when the product changes. That is duplication on purpose; the correspondence
  is listed in the Program.cs header for a reader to check.

  Whether this project is kept after the receive step lands is not settled here.
  If the test design it enables is adopted, the test supersedes it and it may go
  the way of Respond6. If the measurement is one worth repeating on a new machine
  or a new Windows build, it stays, as Listen6 did.

  Common build settings, including the target framework, come from
  Directory.Build.props at the repository root and are not restated here.
-->
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <RootNamespace>SecretPrinter.Loop6</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>SecretPrinter.Loop6</AssemblyName>
    <InvariantGlobalization>true</InvariantGlobalization>
    <!-- Diagnostic only: never packed, never signed, never released. -->
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
